  "worked_solution": "In plain English, our predicate $P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not equal to $5.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. To negate our plain English expression, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is not equal to $5.$\n\nIn other words, $x$ is *equal to* $5.$ Therefore, $¬P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x=5$",
